From 5efa6ebd609f36200b4b87fc21597e59fb834460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:11:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Signed-in nav bar: match the light nav instead of a dark
 coral bar

Pradas's spec: header background #F8F4EA (cream), logo unchanged (it's
already the brand coral, just wasn't visible against the coral bar it
sat on), wordmark text #3F8AB4 (ocean), and the rest of the nav text in
deep navy.

Previously the signed-in nav used a coral gradient background with white
text/translucent-white overlays -- a completely different visual system
from the signed-out nav's light cream bar. Rather than patch that dark
scheme's colors, replaced it: both signed-in and signed-out states now
share one light nav (cream bg, navy link text, coral active-state
highlight, light-surface icon buttons for notifications/profile). The
only thing that still changes based on auth is the "HiBowan" wordmark
color -- ocean blue when signed in, navy when signed out. This also
collapses a lot of user-conditional className branching that existed
only to support the old dark bar.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
